r10earl — Earlgrey_0_1 (Surelog suite, DEFAULT mode) decode witnesses.

run.sh / run2.sh <file.sv>
                   run Surelog (-parse -nocache -mt 0 -mp 0 -d uhdm) and
                   slang-uhdm on the same source and pipe both databases
                   through uhdm-cmp.  run2.sh is the pass-2 copy (edit W= at
                   the top for your worktree).
dmp.sh / dmp2.sh <basename>
                   uhdm-dump both sides of an earlier run into
                   /tmp/r10earl{,2}_rep/out_<b>/{g,o}.dump
tab2.py g.dump o.dump
                   projects each dump onto "(param_assign) -> <decompile>/
                   <size> ..." per view.
pa3.py <dump...>   the same projection with VALUE and CONSTTYPE:
                   "<decompile>/<size>/<value>/<constType>", one field group
                   per view.  This is the one to reach for on a parameter law.
site.py <dump> <lineRegex>
                   every LEAF object at a matching source line, with its
                   cmp-relevant scalars, deduplicated with an xN count — the
                   way to diff two dumps at one declaration.
cmpcsv.py <base.csv> <new.csv> [--dump]
                   status (and dump-column) diff of two verify_golden runs.
sweep.sh <corpus> <mode> <filter> <tag> [jobs]
                   verify_golden wrapper that pins SLANG_UHDM and the workdir.
unsup.sh           replays the Earlgrey slang command line with
                   SLANG_UHDM_UNSUP_LOC=1.
mark.py --on|--off <files...>
                   MARKER-INSTRUMENT every `->VpiDecompile(x)` setter so the
                   emitted text carries an @<FI><LINE> tag naming the site that
                   wrote it.  One build, run the repro, read the tag off the
                   object that is wrong.  This located both pass-2 decompile
                   laws in one build each; do not reason about ~300 sites.
../r10earl2h.cpp   DESIGN-WIDE HEAD CENSUS.  uhdm-cmp names only the FIRST
                   failing pair for the whole design and parameter::Compare
                   recurses Instance(), so one package head masks everything.
                   This Compares each AllModules/TopModules/AllPackages/
                   TopPackages entry against its same-named twin with a FRESH
                   context and prints every head plus its parent chain, so the
                   cluster can be ranked.  AllModules entries have an EMPTY
                   VpiName — they are keyed on vpiDefName.
../r10earl2build.sh <probe-name>   builds a probe against libuhdm.

THE PASS-17 PROBES — READ THIS BEFORE WRITING ANOTHER HAND-ROLLED DESCENT.
Every r10earl probe before pass 17 hand-writes a walk for the node kinds its
author expected, so a difference one level below that imagination is invisible
(that is what left work@tlul_adapter_host "no failing child" for two passes).
These three are GENERIC — they enumerate children through the VPI relation ids
(vpi_handle / vpi_iterate over [1,3000)), so they need no per-type code and
cannot miss a vector:

../r10earl17a.cpp  THE COMPLETE SUB-CENSUS.  r10earl15b enumerates 21 child
        vectors chosen by hand; module_inst::Compare walks FORTY-ONE plus five
        single-object pointers.  17a walks all of them IN COMPARE ORDER, so the
        first non-clean line is the pair uhdm-cmp trips on.  It found
        tlul_adapter_host's failure (Gen_stmts — a vector 15b never looked at)
        in one run.  Driver: sub17.sh <vec> <Listing> [-v].
../r10earl17c.cpp  THE GENERIC BISECTOR — the workhorse of this pass; every
        pass-17 law came out of one of its runs.  CompareContext names the
        failing LEAF; this walks DOWN from a listing child and prints the FIELD
        CHAIN uhdm-cmp follows to reach it, ending either at a NULLNESS report
        ("*** THE MISSING POINTER ***", with both owners' parent chains) or at a
        scalar difference with the full child table.  Driver: bis17.sh <vec>
        <Listing> <selector> — selector = whole | net:/port:/var:/param:/tf: by
        name, ts:/pa:/ca:/proc:/genstmt: by index, refmod:/gsa: by name.
        THREE things it must do, all learned the hard way in this pass:
          * SKIP vpiParent.  It is a pure back-edge; following it walks out of
            the subtree into the design and bisects an unrelated module.
          * SEED each child's CompareContext with the ANCESTOR PATH.  A fresh
            context makes a typespec's Instance() back-edge re-compare the whole
            module and "fail", which is a PHANTOM — the real Compare's m_visited
            makes that edge a no-op.  Children that fail only unseeded are
            printed as CYCLE lines.
          * Key the seen-set on the PAIR, not on the golden node.  One golden
            object pairs with DIFFERENT objects of ours along different paths
            (a shared typespec against per-declaration clones), and a
            golden-only key reports "no child reproduces it" for the very child
            that carries the difference.
../r10earl17d.cpp  THE NULLNESS WALK.  Same generic enumeration with NO Compare
        at all: lockstep both subtrees and report every pointer one side has and
        the other lacks, plus every vector whose sizes differ.  Linear where 17c
        is quadratic; use it when the shape is known to be a missing pointer.
        Driver: nul17.sh.  (It prunes at instance/design boundaries; -deep
        descends anyway.)
../r10earl17b.cpp  subtree dumper over UHDM's own visit_object.  KEPT AS A
        WARNING: visit_object follows Instance() into the whole design, so one
        module_inst produced a 256 MB text file.  Use 17c/17d instead.
../r10earl18a.cpp  THE INSTANCE-TOPNESS CENSUS (pass 18).  The def-vs-top
        re-point family (four pass-16 laws, two pass-17 laws, three pass-18
        laws) all ask the same question of one object at a time; this asks it
        of the WHOLE DESIGN.  It walks the restored arena and prints every
        typespec whose vpiInstance is a PACKAGE as
        `<kind> '<name>' @line:col -> <pkg> top=<0|1>` with an xN count.
        Driver: ins18.sh <tag>, which normalises the file paths away (OUR
        typespecs carry no vpiFile) and prints TWO diffs.  READ THE COUNT DIFF,
        NOT THE SET DIFF: a mis-point keeps both shapes present and only swaps
        the population, so the set diff is silent where the count diff prints
        `prim_pkg::impl_e x1 top=0 / x70 top=1` against our exact inverse.
../r10earl22a.cpp  THE ARENA BIND CENSUS (pass 22).  Every ref_obj whose
        VpiFullName contains <substr> and whose line is in [lo,hi], keyed by
        fullname + line:col, with its Actual_group's TYPE (or `-`) on both
        sides and an ok/DIFF flag.  Where bis22.sh names ONE missing pointer,
        this names ALL of them in a scope at once — which is how pass 22 found
        that ibex_multdiv_fast's `$signed` bind (:147) and its counter-witness
        (:151, same gen block, six lines down, UNBOUND) are the same law, after
        five hand-written witnesses had reproduced neither.  ON A DECODED
        CORPUS HEAD, CENSUS THE CORPUS SCOPE BEFORE BUILDING THE WITNESS.
        Usage: /tmp/r10e22_22a <a.uhdm> <b.uhdm> <fullname-substr> <lo> <hi>.
        Build: bash tools/probe/r10earl22build.sh r10earl22a 22a.  NOTE the
        selector is a FULLNAME substring, never a file suffix: our ELABORATED
        objects carry an empty VpiFile.
        RUN IT OVER THE WHOLE ARENA (pass 23): `"" 0 999999` prints all ~139k
        ref_objs and `grep '^DIFF' | grep -v absent` is then the COMPLETE bind
        residue table for the design, groupable by the G=/O= pair and by
        signal@line — that table is what ranked pass 23 and is also its
        regression check (it shows whether anything NEW started binding).  The
        `<absent>` rows are fullname-PARENT differences, not cmp-relevant.
../r10earl23a.cpp  THE ARENA OBJECT-EXISTENCE CENSUS (pass 23).  22a answers
        "is this ref bound?"; this answers "does this OBJECT EXIST AT ALL, and
        with what type?", which is the question a bisector note like `rel=100
        VECTOR SIZE 20 vs 18` actually asks.  Every object whose VpiFullName
        contains <substr> (and, optionally, whose type name contains
        <typeSubstr>) prints as `G=xN O=xM <type> <fullname> @line:col`.  With
        `"" enum_var` it read pass 23's law-1 family — seven missing enum_var
        DECLARATIONS in the whole design — in one run, after the bisector had
        reported them as a missing POINTER.  CHECK THE OBJECT EXISTS BEFORE
        WRITING A BIND LAW.
        Usage: /tmp/r10e23_23a <a.uhdm> <b.uhdm> <substr> [typeSubstr] [lo] [hi]
        Build: bash tools/probe/r10earl23build.sh r10earl23a 23a.
fcproj18.py <dump...>   projects a uhdm-dump onto its func_call / task_call
        objects — span, vpiName, and whether a vpiFunction / vpiTask binding
        follows — in file order, so the def view and the elab view of the same
        call are separate rows.  This is what read fc18.sv's 3x2 matrix.
run18.sh / dmp18.sh / sweep18.sh / cen18.sh / sub18.sh / bis18.sh / nul18.sh /
        hdiff18.sh / gate18.sh / ins18.sh — the pass-18 harness copies, all
        pointing at THIS worktree.  cen18.sh <tag> is new: one r10earl4h head
        census into /tmp/r10earl18_cen_<tag>.txt plus the four SIZE lines, so
        `cen18.sh l3 && hdiff18.sh ..._l2.txt ..._l3.txt` is the whole
        per-law measurement.
fc18.sv       § defGenQualPkgCallBinds18's matrix: six calls in ONE def-view
        gen_if (cont_assign / always_comb x qualified-package /
        wildcard-imported-package / module-local) plus two module-body
        controls.  Golden binds vpiFunction on exactly the two QUALIFIED rows.
pp18.sv       the § genScopePkgParamRefTop18 shape, kept as a NEGATIVE witness:
        it is cmp-EQUAL both before and after the law, because a package whose
        def and elab copies have IDENTICAL CONTENT compares equal whichever
        copy a pointer names.  A def-vs-top law can only be reproduced in a
        small file if the two copies DIFFER — which is why this family has
        always been decoded on the corpus with the bisector.
