LANDED — PASS 1 (both gated at goldens 23/23 + u2r testflags 0 change +
Surelog both modes 0 change):

  a.sv/d.sv  the adjustSize exemption for BASED literals in a package
        unpacked-array pattern (ParamEmit § the elemSz9 re-stamp).
  b.sv/c.sv  § pkgStringDecompileQuoted — the elab quote-strip on a string
        constant's decompile is a MODULE-elaboration effect.

LANDED — PASS 2 (same gates: goldens 23/23, u2r testflags 0 change incl. the
dump column, Surelog both modes 0 change incl. the dump column):

  f.sv/g.sv/i.sv/j.sv/l.sv  § crossPkgRangeBoundFold (TypeEmit — three helpers
        above makeTypespec + the two hooks in the packed-dim `emitBound`).
        A MODULE parameter's declared-type range bound that names a package
        parameter WITH ITS QUALIFIER is substituted by Surelog's getValue: it
        tokenizes the `::`, finds the package, and hands the read that
        package's own value constant, which then rides reduceExpr like a
        literal.  Decompile / value / constType come across VERBATIM (`8'd6`
        stays `8'd6` with DEC:6), the SIZE is re-stamped to the package
        parameter's DECLARED width unconditionally — based literals included
        (j.sv: 4'd6 at logic[7:0] -> 8, 8'd5 at int -> 32, 4'b1010 at bit[3:0]
        -> 4) — and an UNTYPED package parameter keeps the literal's own width
        and gets an EMPTY ref_typespec rather than none.  The ts ref is named
        after the parameter being declared (`work@m2.PQual`) and its Actual is
        the ELABORATED package's typespec, not the definition package's: the
        two differ only in vpiInstance and typespec::Compare recurses
        Instance(), so pointing at the def package makes the whole package
        unequal from inside an unrelated module (this was Earlgrey
        work@sram2tlul's next head after the fold landed).
        Distinguishers, all measured: a module-LOCAL bound (`logic [W-1:0]`)
        is NOT substituted (g.sv) — an overridable parameter has no value at
        definition-compile time; a VAR/NET declaration bound is not either
        (i.sv row 18); a PACKAGE's own bound is reduced WHOLE by its
        elaboration (`[pa::W-1:0]` -> INT:15, k.sv) and is already right.
        f.sv, g.sv and l.sv (the sram2tlul shape, three files) are BYTE-
        IDENTICAL after this plus the next law.

  h.sv/n.sv/o.sv/p.sv  § unsizedBasedTypedParamElab (ParamEmit, beside the
        DEC-based rewrite it generalises).  The module ELABORATOR rebuilds a
        typed parameter's Rhs from the elaborated VALUE plus the declared
        width, so an UNSIZED BASED default is respelled AT THAT WIDTH; the DEF
        view and both package views keep the raw literal and were already
        right.  Full matrix:
            logic [7:0]  = 'h0   -> 8'h0    HEX  size 8
            logic [15:0] = 'hab  -> 16'hab  HEX  size 16
            int          = 'h9   -> 32'h9   HEX  size 32
            logic [7:0]  = 'sh1f -> 8'h1f   HEX  (the signing `s` drops)
            logic [7:0]  = 'b101 -> 8'b101  BIN  size 8
            logic [7:0]  = 'o10  -> 8       UINT size 8   (OCTAL JOINS
                                                           DECIMAL: the base
                                                           is lost entirely)
            logic [7:0]  = 'd300 -> 300     INT  size 8    (already handled)
        A single-BINARY-DIGIT literal is a SEPARATE GRAMMAR rule (Surelog's
        paNumber_Tickb1): `'b0`/`'b1` carry SIZE 1 and respell as `1'b<d>`
        whatever the declared width is — byte / shortint / longint / integer /
        bit / logic / vector / `int unsigned` all measured (p.sv).  Plain
        signed `int` = `'b1` is the ONE exception (INT:-1 at size 32); `int` =
        `'b0` is not, and `int unsigned` = `'b1` is not.  An UNTYPED parameter
        is untouched (`'h3` stays `'h3` at size -1).

  q.sv  § basedLiteralWsCompact (stripSep, UhdmExporter.h).  The LRM lets
        whitespace sit between the base and the digits (`7'h 0`, `4'd 3` — the
        spelling EVERY OpenTitan reg_pkg offset uses) and Surelog's lexer joins
        the token back together, so no view carries the space.  We stripped
        digit separators there but not whitespace; all 23 callers feed the
        helper based-literal source text, so the two classes strip together.
        Killed ~21 Earlgrey AllModules heads.

  r.sv  § pkgStringDecompileQuoted, keyed on the PHYSICAL view.  §
        modDefImportShape force-sets topView for a module's MATERIALIZED
        IMPORT copies, and that flip leaked into the elab quote-strip.  A
        4-view witness (`module sm import sp::*;` over an UNTYPED
        `parameter ArbiterImpl = "PPC"` and a `string`-typed twin) reads
        quoted / quoted / quoted / bare across pkg-def, pkg-top, module-DEF,
        module-TOP; we stripped the third.  BOTH strip sites need the gate —
        the untyped shape takes the `else if (StringLiteral && !isString())`
        branch, the typed one the general strip.  Killed 14 Earlgrey
        AllModules heads (22 entries reach tlul_pkg's ArbiterImpl).

