LANDED — PASS 3 (r10earl3; every law gated at goldens 23/23 + u2r testflags
0 change + Surelog both modes 0 change, incl. the dump column — four full gate
rounds, one after each law):

  s.sv  § uninstDefPortedAdmit (UhdmExporter exportDesign + ParamEmit
        collectImportedParams).  Surelog's uhdmallModules lists every module
        DEFINITION in the compilation, instantiated or not.  addDefOnlyModule
        already harvested defs reached only through a NON-TAKEN GENERATE
        BRANCH, but admitted them only when PORTLESS; the 13 missing Earlgrey
        entries all have ports.  Dropping the requireNoPorts gate needs ONE
        other fix: InstanceSymbol::createDefault deliberately leaves the
        instance OUT of every scope, so getParentScope() is null and slang's
        resolvePortConnections() — whose SLANG_ASSERT(scope) is compiled out in
        Release — DEREFERENCES THE NULL.  collectImportedParams asks such an
        instance's parentInstance for its port connections; guarded (a def-only
        instance has no instantiator by construction, so there is nothing to
        scan).  Closes AllModules SIZE 190 vs 177 -> 190 vs 190, which was
        masking every per-entry comparison past it; 5 of the 13 new entries are
        cmp-EQUAL immediately.  s.sv is BYTE-IDENTICAL (a ported module and a
        portless one, both instantiated only in the untaken arm).

  u.sv/v.sv/w.sv  § pkgFuncFillSizedInElab (ExprEmit ~2496 + TaskFuncEmit
        pkgSubCalledAsContAssignRhs).  § subCalledAsContAssignRhs — "Surelog
        pushes the assignment size through a call ONLY from a continuous
        assignment whose rhs IS the call" — was implemented with a `!pkgSub9`
        exclusion, measured on rp32's riscv_isa_i_pkg::enc32 whose only caller
        multiplies the call into an operation.  That case never separated
        "package" from "not called that way".  The rule DOES apply to a package
        function, with two extra conditions: only the ELABORATED
        (uhdmtopPackages) copy takes it (the def copy keeps the raw literal),
        and the callers must be found DESIGN-WIDE (a package function has no
        InstanceBody, so the existing helper's home-scope scan can never see
        them).  Full matrix (w.sv, one function per row, all in one package,
        `logic [7:0]` unless stated):
            A no-arg,      `a = '0;`   -> 00000000 / 8
            B one arg,     `b = '0;`   -> 00000000 / 8
            C onto a NET,  `c = '0;`   -> 00000000 / 8
            D              `d = '1;`   -> 11111111 / 8
            E              `e = 'x;`   -> `'X` / -1  (UNKNOWN FILLS NOT SIZED)
            F              `f[0] = '1;`-> `'1` / -1  (bit-select LHS)
            G 128-bit multi-dim, no args -> 128 zeros / 128
            H `return '1;`, DIRECT cont-assign rhs -> `'1` / -1
            I `return '1;`, under an operation     -> `'1` / -1
        and u.sv adds the never-called control: a function with the identical
        body that nothing calls keeps `'0`/-1 in BOTH views.  Corpus:
        aes_pkg::aes_transpose (`transpose = '0;` at logic [3:0][3:0][7:0]),
        reached from 13 Earlgrey AllModules def entries through
        parameter::Compare's Instance() recursion.  u.sv is BYTE-IDENTICAL.

  t.sv  NEGATIVE witness for the law above, kept deliberately: the same `'0`
        shapes in package functions that NOTHING CALLS, plus a package
        parameter, a declaration initialiser, an always_comb body and a
        module-local function.  Golden leaves every one of them `'0`/-1 and so
        do we — t.sv was already cmp-EQUAL before pass 3 and stays so.  It is
        what proved the trigger is the CALL, not the package or the width.

  w.sv rows H/I  § retUnbasedSizing is a MODULE-FUNCTION rule (StmtEmit ~1968).
        A PACKAGE function's `return '1;` keeps the raw literal at -1 in BOTH
        package views however the function is called; we sized it to the return
        width in both.  Gated on pkgScopeInst (set exactly for a package's own
        non-class subroutines, in both views).

  x.sv  § syntaxMultiConcat (TypeEmit emitSyntaxExpr).  The syntax-driven
        expression emitter — which builds a module-DEF gen block's whole
        subtree — had a ConcatenationExpression arm but NO
        MultipleConcatenationExpression arm, so `{N{x}}` returned null and the
        replication VANISHED from its enclosing concat: `{1'b1,{(PW-1){1'b0}}}`
        came out as a ONE-operand concat.  The same replication in a PROCEDURAL
        statement of the same gen block was already right (that path is
        AST-emitted) — which is why this survived so long.  Surelog's shape is a
        vpiMultiConcatOp spanning the OUTER braces over [count, inner concat],
        the inner concat a plain vpiConcatOp at its own braces.  Corpus:
        prim_fifo_sync.sv:110 `assign full = (fifo_wptr == (fifo_rptr ^
        {1'b1,{(PTR_WIDTH-1){1'b0}}}));` — 13 AllModules def entries, which then
        ADVANCED to the y.sv head in the same file.

  y.sv  § syntaxUnsizedBasedSize (TypeEmit emitSyntaxExpr, same arm).  The
        syntax emitter gave EVERY unsized based literal SIZE 64 (the
        bare-decimal width).  Golden's def and elab views agree row for row:
            'b0 -> 0    'b1 -> 0   (paNumber_Tickb0/Tickb1, the separate grammar
                                    nodes the AST arm already decodes as
                                    tickBinDigit — normalised lowercase
                                    decompile, hard-coded SIZE 0)
            'b101 -> -1   'h3 -> -1   'o7 -> -1   'd9 -> -1   'bx -> -1
            8'hab -> 8   (SIZED control)
        Also moved stripSep AHEAD of the size parse in that arm so a
        whitespace-separated literal measures the same as a compact one.
        Corpus: prim_fifo_sync.sv:145 `assign rdata = empty ? 'b0 : rdata_int;`
        — the same 13 entries.  y.sv is BYTE-IDENTICAL.

