  METHOD HEADLINE, and it cost this pass two wrong turns: **MEASURE THE
  MEASURER.**  The census script written to read bind-ness out of a uhdm-dump
  stopped its forward scan at the next `operation:` line — but a ref_obj's own
  `|vpiParent: \_operation:` is printed BEFORE `|vpiActual:`, so EVERY ref with
  an operation parent read as unbound.  On that evidence this pass first
  "refuted" pass 21's hier_path counter-witness and wrote it up as a mis-read;
  uhdm-cmp then printed the enum_const golden binds at dut.sv:91:59 in one
  line.  The fixed script is INDENTATION-BASED (attributes are the lines at
  exactly refIndent+2) and it is what every measurement below rests on.  When a
  census contradicts uhdm-cmp, the census is wrong.

  1. § genCaEnumBindsSelectOnly22 (ExprEmit ~4990, + genCaLhsSelect22 in
     UhdmExporter.h / ModuleEmit ~12527).  Pass 21's refuted
     § genCaEnumConstNoBind21, landed once the missing quarter of its 2x2 was
     measured.  IN A GEN-SCOPE CONT-ASSIGN RHS AN ENUM-CONST REF BINDS ONLY
     WHEN (a) the ref is in a SELECT POSITION — part-select bound, bit-select
     index, or inside an index OPERATION — OR (b) THE CONT-ASSIGN'S LHS IS
     ITSELF A SELECT.  qa22.sv is one design of nine gen-scope rows over a
     wildcard-imported package enum plus three module-level controls: golden
     leaves the ternary BRANCHES (:61:30/:36), the ternary's own COMPARISON
     CONDITION (:61:23), a bare comparison (:62:23), a branch one operation
     deeper (:68:22/:28/:35) and the same comparison in a FOR-generate
     (:72:23) all UNBOUND, and binds the part-select bounds (:63/:64), the
     bit-select index (:65) and all three MODULE-level rows.
     (b) IS WHAT PASS 21 WAS MISSING and it is why its blanket widening
     regressed exactly two u2r rows: hier_path assigns
     `region_start_addr[r]` / `region_addr_mask[r][b]` and
     MultirangesStartNotFromZero assigns `io_fwd_link_li[i][e_e:w_e]` — SELECT
     LHS, every one — while the Earlgrey head and every qa22 no-bind row
     assign a PLAIN NAME (ibex_id_stage.sv:911, `assign instr_type_wb_o =
     ~lsu_req_dec ? WB_INSTR_OTHER : ...`).  The $unit carve-out is untouched.
     THE PARENT TEST HAS TO NAME part_select / indexed_part_select /
     var_select as well as bit_select: the FLATTENED select path (an element
     select THEN a range, `x[i][e_e:w_e]`) sets neither inPsBound nor
     selIdxScopeDepth — found as the Multiranges regression in gate round 0.
  2. § genCaSelEnumPlainDecompile22 (ExprEmit, at the clone mint).  The fresh
     enum_const clone minted for a SELECT-POSITION survivor of law 1 carries
     the PLAIN DECIMAL decompile: qa22 :63/:64/:65 are `2`/`2`/`1` where the
     shared consts read `2'd2`/`3'd2`/`2'd1`, and Multiranges' `e_e` bound is
     INT:2 decompile `2` at size 3.  THE SELECT-POSITION GATE IS LOAD-BEARING,
     not plain inGenScopeCaRhs: hier_path's LHS-select survivor at :91:59 is a
     comparison operand and golden keeps the sized `2'b01` there.
  3. § elabCaTernaryFoldIntConst22 (ModuleEmit ~18490).  A CONSTANT-CONDITION
     ternary cont-assign RHS reduces to vpiIntConst (INT:), ALWAYS — not only
     when the value is negative, which is all the previous code encoded.
     qc22.sv's five folding rows are INT:5/INT:0/INT:0/INT:5/INT:9, all
     non-negative, all ct=7.  Corpus: ibex_alu.sv:244 `assign bfp_op = RV32B ?
     (operator_i == ALU_BFP) : 1'b0;` with `parameter bit RV32B = 1'b0`,
     golden {ct=7 sz=1 dec=0} where we emitted ct=9 — pass 20's residue (6),
     the dm_mem "ct7-vs-ct9 family".  A constant OPERATION RHS with no ternary
     above it keeps vpiUIntConst (qb22 `assign t7 = 4'h7 | 4'h8` -> UINT:15
     ct=9), so this is the conditional reduce's own encoding.
  4. § elabCaTernaryNoFoldSigRefBranch22 (ModuleEmit ~18265 + ~18490).  That
     reduce happens ONLY WHEN NEITHER BRANCH IS A BARE SIGNAL REFERENCE.
     qb22.sv confounded result WIDTH with the shape of the not-taken branch;
     qc22.sv crosses them and WIDTH IS NOT THE FEATURE:
       P ? (a & 4'h3) : 4'd5        FOLDS (4-bit)   P ? b : 1'b0   KEEPS (1-bit)
       P ? a[0]       : 1'b0        FOLDS (1-bit)   P ? a : 1'b1   KEEPS (4-bit)
       P ? (4'h3&4'h1): 4'h9        FOLDS           P ? a : (4'h3|4'h8) KEEPS
     A bare ref_obj operand is the one thing Surelog's reduce treats as a HARD
     failure (an operation it cannot fold is handed back un-reduced), and one
     anywhere in the conditional abandons the whole reduce; a BIT-SELECT of the
     same signal does not.  BOTH FOLD PATHS have to honour it — tryFoldConst
     catches the sized-literal arms, the dedicated ternary reduce catches the
     `'0` arm, and gating only the second left three of five rows still folded.
  5. § genCaSysCallArgBinds22 (ExprEmit ~4840 + sysCallArgDepth22 around the
     sys-call arg loop; + the deep20 walk in ModuleEmit now descends through
     sys_func_call).  A ref NESTED INSIDE a SYSTEM function call's argument in
     an elab gen-scope cont_assign RHS BINDS, regardless of the LHS.  qf22.sv
     writes ibex_multdiv_fast.sv:147 verbatim into a child instance and
     reproduces the corpus row for row (`$signed({mult1_sign_a, mult1_op_a}) *
     $signed({...})` — all four concat operands bound in golden, none in ours).
     qe22.sv separates the features: the module-LHS row `assign my =
     $signed({s1,v1})` binds too (so it is not the gen-local-LHS rule reaching
     further) while `assign oy = mult1_res ^ pv_res` stays unbound (so it is
     not a blanket module-LHS bind); qd22.sv is the TOP-module control where
     all of them already bind through the unsuppressed path — THE LAW IS A
     CHILD-INSTANCE GAP, which is why five passes of top-module witnesses never
     saw it.  THE `parent != sys_func_call` TEST IS THE COUNTER-WITNESS'S: four
     lines below the head golden leaves `assign mac_res_signed =
     $signed(summand1) + $signed(summand2) + $signed(summand3);` (:151) and
     `assign mac_res_ext = $unsigned(mac_res_signed);` (:153) COMPLETELY
     unbound — same gen scope, same `$signed`, but a BARE-REF argument under a
     MODULE-level LHS.  A bare argument under a GEN-LOCAL LHS does bind
     (qe22 `assign r1 = $signed(v1)`), and that half is the deep20 extension.
  7. § genCaSysCallTsVarLhs22 (ModuleEmit ~12690).  The gen-scope sys-call RHS
     typespec stamp accepted only a logic_NET LHS, so a MODULE-level `logic`
     signal that no module-level cont_assign drives (slang and Surelog both
     keep it a Variable) silently lost the stamp when its only driver sat in a
     gen scope.  qg22.sv G6 `assign me = $unsigned(ms);` is the isolation — its
     four sibling rows, all PORT (logic_net) LHS, already stamped.  Corpus:
     ibex_multdiv_fast.sv:153 with `logic [34:0] mac_res_ext;` at :52.
  8. § genCaLiteralRhsLhsNoBind22 (ModuleEmit ~12758 lhsSuppress arm AND the
     bindGenLocal9(Lhs) call ~12960).  A gen-scope cont_assign whose RHS is a
     bare LITERAL leaves its OWN-SCOPE gen-local LHS ref UNBOUND.  qf22 rows:
       assign mult1_sign_a = 1'b0;          LHS UNBOUND in golden
       assign mult1_op_a  = op_a_i[15:0];   LHS bound
       assign mult1_res   = $signed(..)*..; LHS bound
     and the corpus agrees object for object — ibex_multdiv_fast's three
     `= 1'b0` assignments (:161/:162/:167) are the ONLY gen-local LHS refs
     golden leaves unbound in that whole gen scope.  TWO WRITERS: gating only
     the bindGenLocal9 fallback changed nothing, then gating only the emit
     changed nothing either, because each re-wrote what the other dropped.
     (Numbering keeps the in-code § names; there is no law 6.)

