  THE METHOD HEADLINE: **A LAW THAT ONLY EVER SAW ONE SPELLING IS A LAW WITH AN
  UNMEASURED HALF.**  Every one of this pass's five laws is a REACH correction
  to an existing § law whose original witness confounded two features:
    * § genCaDirectRefBindsGenLocal said a gen-scope cont_assign binds a
      gen-local ref only as the WHOLE Rhs, "not inside an operation" — but the
      tk.sv row that clause came from read an ANCESTOR scope's local, which the
      same file separately proved is unbound whole-ref or not.
    * § genProcParamFold said "Surelog's reduce does not descend into call
      actuals" — every callee in r10scr14repro/t6.sv is module-local.
    * § tfFormalTs said a formal's range bound folds like a module one — its
      witness writes the range inline; a formal typed by a TYPEDEF does not.
  Write the 2x2 (or 2x3) that separates the features BEFORE writing the code:
  three of the five laws below came out of a single purpose-built file each.

  1. § genCaOpDeepBindGenLocal20 (ModuleEmit, after the bindGenLocal9 pair;
     round 1).  Pass-19 residue (1), a ONE-POINTER head.  In an ELABORATED gen
     scope, a cont_assign whose LHS is a variable declared in THIS gen block
     binds EVERY same-scope gen-local variable ref anywhere in its Rhs, at any
     operand depth.  ps20.sv is the isolation, three rows of one gen block:
       assign s1 = v1 ^ 4'h5;   Lhs GEN-LOCAL,  Rhs operation -> BOUND
       assign y1 = v1 ^ 4'h5;   Lhs MODULE net, Rhs operation -> unbound
       assign y2 = v1;          Lhs MODULE net, Rhs whole ref -> BOUND
     THE LHS IS THE DISCRIMINATOR.  pq20.sv adds the negatives that survive
     (a module-level signal and an ancestor-scope local read from inside the
     operation both stay unbound) and pr20.sv kills the two confounds — operand
     DEPTH and process- vs cont_assign-driven are both irrelevant.  Corpus:
     work@prim_prince's `assign data_state_xor = data_state_round ^ ...`
     (:105:29), whose Rhs ref was the ONLY nullness in 426 node pairs.
     REGRESSION-DERIVED CARVE-OUT (gate round 1, u2r genvar_loop_decl_3
     CMP_EQUAL -> CMP_NOTEQUAL): the LHS does not count as gen-local when its
     NAME is also declared at MODULE level.  px20.sv is the three-way bisect —
     the test's own module verbatim (unbound), the same module with the two gen
     locals RENAMED so nothing shadows (BOUND), and the shadowing kept but the
     module-level hierarchical reads removed (unbound).  The proof is in
     golden's own pointer: the shadowed Lhs `y` binds `logic_net work@gate.y`,
     the MODULE net — Surelog never resolved it to the gen-local at all, so by
     law 1's own rule the assignment does not target that gen scope.
  2. § genProcParamFoldQualCallArg20 (ExprEmit ~4534 + a new qualCallArg20
     flag saved/restored around the func_call arg loop; round 2).  The
     call-actual exception is the UNQUALIFIED-CALL exception.  pu20.sv puts one
     module parameter under four calls in one elab gen-scope process: golden
     folds it under the three written `pu20_pkg::pf(...)` / `pu20_pkg::pi(...)`
     and keeps `ref_obj IDX` under the WILDCARD-IMPORTED, unqualified `pf(...)`.
     THE WRITTEN QUALIFIER IS THE DISCRIMINATOR — pass 18 § defGenQualPkgCall-
     Binds18 and pass 19 laws 3-4 in a fourth container.  pt20.sv is the
     6-row companion (unpacked port vs packed 2-D var x bare / local call /
     package call).  Corpus: work@prim_prince :116:67,
     `prim_cipher_pkg::sbox4_64bit(data_state[NumRoundsHalf], ...)`.
  3. § genProcParamFoldTopGenOnly20 (ExprEmit, same exception list; round 2).
     The fold is a TOP-LEVEL gen scope's privilege.  pv20.sv puts the same
     parameter in an always_comb of a flat if-generate, a flat for-generate, an
     if-generate NESTED in a for-generate and an if-generate NESTED in an
     if-generate: golden folds the two FLAT ones and keeps the ref in both
     nested ones, LOOP OR NO LOOP, so the discriminator is GENERATE NESTING
     DEPTH.  (A named_begin inside the process is a STATEMENT block and does
     not count.)  Corpus: prim_prince folds :116:67 in the flat
     `gen_middle_d64` and keeps :150:20 in `gen_bwd_d64`, nested inside
     `gen_bwd_pass`.  Laws 2+3 together CLOSED work@prim_prince (Top).
  4+5. § modTdRetCloneSymbolic20, both halves (TaskFuncEmit ~1819 for the
     RETURN clone and ~2472 for the FORMAL clone; round 3).  A function's
     return typed by a MODULE-LOCAL scalar typedef, and a FORMAL typed by one,
     each get a fresh clone — built without tfContext, so the clone folds the
     typedef's range where golden keeps it symbolic.  The PACKAGE branch right
     above already does this (§ pkgTdRangeViewFold18 sets
     `tfContext = pkgTdOwnDefView(...)`); the module-local branch never did.
     pz20.sv is the witness and bisects to the corpus head's exact field chain
     (cont_assign > func_call > function > Return logic_var / io_decl >
     ref_typespec > logic_typespec 'box_t' > Ranges[2] > Left_expr, golden
     `operation {op=11}` = `W-1`, ours `constant 63`).  THE RETURN HALF ALONE
     MEASURED A BYTE-IDENTICAL CENSUS — and was not a zero: re-running the
     bisector showed the head had moved from `bitarray_to_box`'s return to
     `theta`'s io_decl, the SAME law one object over (pass 19's method note,
     third occurrence).  def:work@prim_keccak CLOSED.

