     clone is UNPARENTED, so modOwnedTs15's vpiParent walk dies on it and
     repointModOwnedTs16 leaves its Typedef_alias naming the DEF package.
     READ OWNERSHIP OFF THE BINDING REF, not off the clone.  The alias fix
     alone measured a byte-identical head census — and was NOT a zero: the
     bisect had advanced from `rel=701 r=-32` to `rel=745 NULLNESS`, i.e. the
     SECOND pointer in the same object (the clone's own vpiInstance, which
     makeTypespec never sets).  Filling that null too closed work@sha2 and
     advanced work@hmac.  THE PASS-16 TWO-POINTER LESSON IN A THIRD GUISE, and
     a metric lesson: hdiff19's failLhs/failRhs was IDENTICAL across the
     advance, because the head's first failing pair was already the same
     `package hmac_pkg {top=1}` / `<null>` one level up.  When a law is
     believed and measures zero, RE-RUN THE BISECTOR, not the census.
     Counted proof of no over-fire: ins19's count diff moved exactly ONE row,
     `logic_typespec 'sha_word_t' :17:11 x16 -> x17 top=1`, toward golden.
  2. § genForCondQualPkgParamFold19 (ModuleEmit, the gen_for pkgLoopParam
     lambda; round 2).  The whole gen-for bound fold resolves through
