  THE NEW TOOL IS THE HEADLINE.  Pass 17 gave the bisector; pass 18 adds the
  DESIGN-WIDE METRIC that ranks its findings.  tools/probe/r10earl18a.cpp walks
  the whole restored arena and prints, for every typespec whose vpiInstance is
  a PACKAGE, `<kind> '<name>' @line:col -> <pkg> top=<0|1>` with an xN count;
  ins18.sh diffs golden's listing against ours.  THE COUNTS ARE THE METRIC, not
  the SET: a def-vs-top mis-point leaves both shapes present and only swaps how
  many objects sit on each, so the set diff prints nothing while the count diff
  prints `prim_pkg::impl_e x1/x70 top=0/1` against golden's `x70/x1` — the
  entire pass-17 residue (2), exactly inverted, in one line.  This is how a
  re-point law is now VERIFIED (law 1 below took its family from 70/1 wrong to
  70/1 right) instead of inferred from a head that moved.

  1. § modParamEnumClonePkgTopInstance18 (TypeEmit, modTdClonePkgTopInstance16
