§ pkgTypespecInstanceIsTop IS NOW MOSTLY CLOSED, and it was never ONE pointer.
Pass 15 left it as "which package copy does a module typespec name"; the
answer is that a module listing reaches the same package through FOUR
independent pointers, and fixing fewer than all of them measures as ZERO —
which is exactly why pass 15's Elem_typespec descent looked like a dead end.
Failing CHILDREN across the eleven sub-censused listings: 100 (pass-15 exit)
-> 64 -> 62 -> 45.  Heads stay 33; the head line hides all of it.

  1. § modPkgTdTopDescend16 (TypeEmit, beside modPkgTypedefTopTs15).  The
     parent walk modPkgTypedefTopTs15 uses can never reach a binding whose
     ref_typespec hangs under an UNPARENTED WRAPPER — a port declared
     `prim_alert_pkg::alert_rx_t [NumAlerts-1:0] alert_rx_i` gets a
     packed_array_typespec minted at :0:0 with no vpiParent.  So descend from
     every module / interface / program listing MEMBER (nets, variables,
     parameters, ports, the listing's own Typespecs, cont_assigns) through the
     wrapper's Elem_typespec chain, the range bounds hanging off it and the
     EXPRESSION trees inside those bounds.  PASS 15's MEASURED ZERO IS
     REFUTED, and the refutation is a measurement: an instrumented
     modPkgTypedefTopTs15 prints
     `TDMAP name='prim_alert_pkg::alert_rx_t' defuid=4152 topuid=21622`, so
     the def->top pairing DID contain the struct all along (the ParamEmit
     listing-loop tail registers every typedef kind).  Alone the descent moves
     ONE child (rv_dm Nets[17] `hartinfo`) — see law 2 for why.
  2. § pkgParamTsTopInstance16 (TypeEmit; called from UhdmExporter right after
     modPkgTypedefTopTs15).  THE LAW THAT OWNED THE -32 HEADS.  A module
     expression that SUBSTITUTES a package parameter's value — every
     `logic [NumAlerts-1:0]` bound, every folded cross-package read — emits a
     CONSTANT, and expr::Compare walks that constant's Typespec, whose
     typespec::Compare then recurses Instance().  We pointed the constant at
     the DEFINITION package's parameter typespec; golden mints a fresh
     int_typespec per site and instances it at the ELABORATED package
     (r10earl16a on work@hmac `alerts`: `TS int_typespec hmac_pkg.sv:10:14
     inst=package hmac_pkg {top=1}` vs ours `{top=0}`).  Only the INSTANCE is
     cmp-relevant, so re-pointing at the elaborated package's own parameter
     typespec is equivalent to golden's fresh object.  Pairing: same-named
     package in AllPackages (def) / TopPackages (elab), parameters by name.
     With law 1: 100 -> 64 children.  hmac Ports[7]/[8] + Nets[78] +
     Cont_assigns[43], ALL 13 of usbdev's r=25 nets (residue item 2 CLOSED),
     all 10 padring r=12 ports, all 8 flash_phy_core r=-601 children,
     dm_mem's 3 Param_assigns; dm_mem's head advanced -32 -> -2.
  3. § modTdClonePkgTopInstance16 (TypeEmit; after LAW S and
     importCloneBareTdAlias16, which are the last writers of a module
     listing's typespec clones).  A net declared as a PACKED VECTOR OF a
     package typedef (`sha_word_t [7:0] digest`) binds NO listing object at
     all: the emitter mints a PER-DECLARATION CLONE of the typedef and hangs
     it off the outer logic_typespec's Elem_typespec.  Two of the clone's
     fields point into the def package — its own vpiInstance (copied from the
     object it was made of) and its Typedef_alias TARGET — and
     typespec::Compare walks BOTH.  There is no def->top pair to re-point for
     the clone itself, so its Instance is re-STAMPED and its alias target is
     re-pointed at the elaborated package's listing twin (paired by name +
     UhdmType inside a package pair).  Guard: a typespec that IS a listing
     object (any package's Typespecs entry, any package parameter's typespec,
     any typedefTs / pkgTopTypedefTs value) is shared and never touched.
     64 -> 62: hmac `digest`, sha2 `w` / `hash` / `wipe_v` / Process[1],
     Process[0] -32 -> 1.
  4. § pkgRefActualTopParam16 (TypeEmit; the map is built by law 2's package
     pairing, the re-point lives in the descent's walkExpr).  The FOURTH
     pointer: an UNFOLDED package-parameter read (`logic [top_pkg::TL_AIW-1:0]
     tl_source`) keeps a ref_obj, and ref_obj::Compare walks Actual_group —
     ours named the DEF package's parameter, golden the elaborated one
     (r10earl16a prints `ACTUAL parameter 'TL_AIW' / OWNER package 'top_pkg'
     {top=1}` against `{top=0}`).  62 -> 45, the single biggest step:
     work@tlul_adapter_host's ENTIRE child list (8) empties and its head goes
     -32 -> -12; tlul_adapter_sram's four -32 nets, `rmask`, two cont_assigns
     and Typespecs[1] all clear; dm_mem loses 5 more (3 ports, `progbuf`,
     Cont_assigns[13]); rv_dm loses its 3 -32 nets.

