PASS-16 OPS NOTES
  * A RE-POINT LAW THAT FIXES ONE OF TWO POINTERS MEASURES AS ZERO.  Pass 15
    reverted a correct traversal because the object it fixed was still reached
    through a second pointer into the same wrong package.  Before believing a
    "measured zero", re-run the probe on the object the law touched and check
    whether it MOVED — hmac's port element did move in pass 15 and the head
    did not.  A law's yield and a law's correctness are different questions.
  * ASK WHAT Compare ACTUALLY WALKS.  Every law in this pass came from reading
    UHDM's generated `*::Compare` in ~/git-repos/UHDM/build/generated/src/:
    expr::Compare walks Typespec (so EVERY constant reaches a package),
    ref_obj::Compare walks Actual_group, typespec::Compare walks Typedef_alias
    AND Instance, logic_typespec::Compare walks Elem_typespec.  Four reads,
    four laws.  Guessing which field carried the difference cost pass 15 a
    whole cycle.
  * AN INSTRUMENTED EMITTER BEATS A THEORY ABOUT A MAP.  Twelve lines of
    getenv-gated fprintf inside modPkgTypedefTopTs15 refuted pass 15's central
    claim in one build.  When a law's premise is "the map does not contain
    X", print the map.

