THE DECODE THAT MATTERS — § pkgTypespecInstanceIsTop IS A POINTER QUESTION AND
THE CLASS IS BIGGER THAN THE HEAD LIST SAID.  Pass 13 named the linking object
and pass 14 built the probe that prints it, and both stalled because the head
line only ever shows the END of the walk (`package 'dm' {top=1}` vs
`{top=0}`, or `package 'top_pkg' {top=1}` vs `<null>`).  Three measurements
settle it:

  1. r10earl15b's `def2top` mode, run on the GOLDEN ALONE and then on OURS
     ALONE, shows both databases' own AllPackages/TopPackages copies of
     hmac_pkg differing IDENTICALLY (`AlertAsyncOn`'s logic_typespec range
     bound: a folded constant in the top copy, the operation in the def one).
     So nothing is wrong with either package copy — only with WHICH ONE a
     module's typespec points at.
  2. The 2 `constant dm_pkg.sv:29:43 {ct=9 sz=64 dec=2052}` vs operation heads
     (dm_mem, rv_dm), ranked for four passes as a same-package localparam FOLD
     bug, are NOT a fold bug: r10earl15b prints the parent chain
     `^ param_assign ^ package 'dm' {top=1 uid=16} ^ design` against
     `{top=0 uid=5892}`.  dm_mem contains NO import at all — every reference
     is `dm::` — which is exactly why no fold rule ever fitted.  wf.sv, built
     to reproduce the "package localparam reads a same-package localparam"
     shape, came back with EVERY param_assign identical in all four listings
     (only topModules SPANS differ, and paspan14 already proved spans are not
     cmp-relevant): the witness is a MEASURED NEGATIVE and the head belongs to
     this class.  The class is 8 heads, not 6.
  3. r10earl15c names the objects.  work@hmac's `InitHash` differs from golden
     in ONE field of ONE node — the array_typespec's ELEMENT
     `logic_typespec 'sha_word_t'`, `inst=` top=1 vs top=0, every other field
     byte-identical.  Its nets differ only in their typespec's Typedef_alias
     TARGET.  Its port `alert_rx_i` differs only in the Instance of
     `prim_alert_pkg::alert_rx_t` and of all four of its members.

  wg.sv / wh.sv are the two MEASURED NEGATIVES from trying to reproduce this
  in a witness: wh.sv (a three-package chain — module port of `whp::t_t`,
  whose members are ranged by `whq::W` — the tlul_pkg/top_pkg shape hmac
  reaches) and wg.sv (dm_mem's shape: NO import, qualified `wgp::` reads, a
  package struct and enum as port/var types, a package function call) are
  BOTH cmp-EQUAL on the typespec Instances.  Do not spend another pass on a
  synthetic witness for this class; work the corpus with r10earl15b/15c.

