  wc.sv  § impCondBranchFold (ParamEmit ~10700, the § impArithFoldSigned
        block).  THE WHOLE RULE IS "reduce the ternary chain, then re-ask this
        block's existing question": Surelog's reduce substitutes the TAKEN
        BRANCH first (the lazy semantics § lazyTernary9 already models for the
        elab view), so fold-or-not, INT-vs-UINT and the anchor span are all
        read off the SELECTED BRANCH, never off the ternary.  wc.sv is one row
        per branch shape, read in the DEF listing of work@wcnp (an importer
        with NO parameter port list — the shape that reaches this site; the
        wcpp twin, WITH a port list, already folded and differed only in span):
            T1 `WM==1 ? 1 : LB`      UINT:1 ct9 @19:36  branch leaf
            T2 `WM==1 ? 1 : 7`       UINT:7 ct9 @20:36  literal leaf
            T3 `WM==2 ? LB : 9`      UINT:1 ct9 @21:32  cond TRUE, span moves
                                                        LEFT
            T5 `WM==1 ? 1 : LB - 1`  INT:0  ct7 @26:36  the BRANCH's own `-`
                                                        decides signedness AND
                                                        the left-operand anchor
            T6 `WM==1 ? 1 : LB + 1`  UINT:2 ct9 @27:36  `+` control
            T4 `WM / 2`              unchanged (negative control)
        Corpus flash_phy_pkg.sv:43.  flash_phy_rd_buffers CLOSED end to end;
        flash_phy_rd advanced.  36 -> 35.

  wd.sv  § caOpFoldTs (ExprEmit ~3657 + the caFold9 clone test).  The
        def-view cont-assign stamp fired only when the fold's parent WAS the
        cont_assign (`assign x = P;`).  It is not a parent test at all: golden
        stamps EVERY fold of an unqualified imported package parameter that a
        DEF-view cont-assign RHS reduces, at any operation depth above it —
        § procOpFold9 / § tfOpFold9 / § ndaOpFold9 are the same law already
        recorded for the process, subroutine-body and net-decl-assign
        containers, and the plain cont-assign one was the hole.  wd.sv rows,
        DEF listing of work@wdnp:
            R1 `{NB{req_i}} & buf_alloc`  count TWO ops deep   -> stamp
            R5 `NB + 8'h1`                operand one op deep  -> stamp
            R6 `{NB{req_i}}`              count one op deep    -> stamp
            R2 `{ML{req_i}}`  module localparam — NEGATIVE control, never folds
