        (`input vq_t [PI-1:0] s_i` after `import vqp::*`) reproduced BOTH
        sub-shapes at once and they are ONE law.  The def-listing bound over a
        NAMED (struct/enum typedef) element keeps its `op11 { <ident>, 1 }`
        tree, but only the MODULE-parameter half of it: a leaf naming a PACKAGE
        parameter is already valued when the def compiles, so Surelog
        substitutes the value exactly as the plain-`logic` def-net arm does —
        UINT at the parameter's DECLARED width with a bare (fullname-less) ts
        ref to the parameter's own typespec.  The 2x2 vq measured:
            row S  `vq_t [PI-1:0]`  op11{constant 4/32/UINT ct9 +ts, 1}
            row T  `vq_t [PI:0]`    constant 4/32/UINT ct9 +ts (NO operation
                                    is built at all, so the plain spelling
                                    needs its own return)
            row Q3 `logic [MP-1:0]` ref_obj(MP) — the module-parameter twin,
                                    UNCHANGED (negative control)
        vq's SIZE table is the general rule behind pass-12 ranked (1)(b) as
        well: a PLAIN parameter-reference bound is sized at the parameter's
        DECLARED type (int -> 32, `logic [7:0]` -> 8, `byte` -> 8, UNTYPED ->
        64), never the bare 64 makeBoundConst writes; an ARITHMETIC bound is a
        64-bit ct7 computed value.  Corpus: alert_handler (CLOSED end to end),
        hmac, flash_ctrl:310 and tlul_adapter_host/top_pkg:8 (the sz-32-vs-64
        pair).  39 -> 38.

