  vr.sv  § defNetBoundPkgIntEnc (TypeEmit ~8440 defNetTsScope arm +
        pkgBoundValueConst9).  4 heads, and the LAST difference on two modules.
        A substituted package-parameter value is a SIGNED INT constant (ct7)
        when that parameter's OWN initializer is arithmetic in the existing
        paramIntEnc sense (`%`, `/`, a signed `**`, or the `X-1` subtract
        form) and a UINT one (ct9) otherwise.  vr rows H1 vs H4 are the
        measurement — the SAME `logic [N-1:0]` net bound, `vrp::NE = 12` giving
        UINT:12 and `vrp::NC = PW - 1` giving INT:16 — and the corpus confirms
        both directions: rstmgr_pkg's `OffDomains = PowerDomains-1` reads ct7 in
        every position golden substitutes it (rstmgr_ctrl:31 net bound,
        rstmgr_ctrl:64 process part-select width), while flash_ctrl_pkg's
        `AddrW = BankW + PageW + WordW` — an ADD, which paramIntEnc does NOT
        mark — stays ct9 and is why flash_erase_ctrl:41 closed with UINT one
        round earlier.  37 -> 36 (rstmgr_ctrl CLOSED end to end).

