PASS-13 OPS NOTES
  * The Earlgrey default sweep costs ~5 SECONDS with a warm golden cache, and
    the census another ~30.  That makes "edit, build -j3, sweep, census, hdiff"
    a ~4-minute loop and there is NO reason to batch laws; five gate rounds
    cost less than one pass-8 round did.
  * hdiff13.sh is the whole measurement (pass 12 said this; now it is a
    script).  An ADVANCED head is a NEW DATUM: five of pass 13's advances
    handed over the next sub-arm of the same law for free (net bound -> param
    Rhs -> $clog2 argument -> process expression -> const type).
  * Build the witness ROW the previous pass names, not the one the head text
    suggests.  vq.sv row S was written from pass 12's one-line "its element
    type is a STRUCT TYPEDEF — BUILD THAT ROW FIRST" and it cracked a class
    that had survived two passes.
  * A three-value witness beats a two-value one.  vr.sv folds 17 where the
    module says 10; had both been 8 (as in flash_mp, where module and package
    both say 8) the measurement would have proved nothing about WHICH
    declaration Surelog reads.  Pick shadow values that DISAGREE.

