NEW TOOL (pass 11):
  ../r10earl11p.cpp  WHO LINKS TO THIS PACKAGE?  A § pkgTypespecInstanceIsTop
                     head reads "package X {top=1} vs {top=0}" with the DESIGN
                     as its whole parent chain, so neither a dump nor the
                     census can name the object that reached the wrong copy.
                     This walks ONE named AllModules entry with UhdmListener
                     and prints the CALLSTACK of every visit to a package of
                     the wanted name.  Usage:
                       r10earl11p <a.uhdm> <ModuleDefName> <PackageName>
                     The one trick that makes it work: insert the DESIGN into
                     getVisited() before listenAny(), or the walk climbs
                     VpiParent into it and reaches every package trivially.
                     It located § pkgFormalTsElabTwin in one run (the chain
                     ref_obj 'lfsr_state' -> ref_typespec -> logic_typespec
