READ THIS FIRST: PASS 8's `gen_host_fifo` DECODE WAS WRONG, AND THE WRONG
DECODE SURVIVED TWO PASSES AS THE #1 RANKED LEAD.  It said golden's def-view
gen block carries "one more statement" because tlul_socket_m1.sv:101 is a
macro-expanded CONCURRENT ASSERTION.  It is not: `ASSERT` expands to nothing
unless INC_ASSERT is defined and Earlgrey never defines it, so BOTH sides emit
nothing for line 101.  r10earl10g (which prints a named_begin's Stmts vector
side by side, i.e. names the missing statement instead of guessing at it) says
the missing statement is line 90, `tlul_pkg::tl_h2d_t hreq_fifo_i;`.  The
lesson is the one the pass-9 record already drew for the ref_obj family: when
a head says "vector SIZE mismatch", PRINT THE TWO VECTORS before theorising
about which member is missing.

  va.sv  § defGenQualTypedefDecl (ModuleEmit emitDefGenStmts, the
        DataDeclaration loop).  A declaration whose type is written WITH A
        PACKAGE QUALIFIER stmt-ifies in the DEF view with its type RESOLVED —
        the package is compiled before the module definition is, so Surelog
        binds the package's own typespec object.  Matrix (va.sv, one
        declaration per row, golden's def-view gen block):
            vap::vs_t       sA   struct_var -> struct_typespec 'vap::vs_t'
            vs_t            sB   NOTHING    (bare, wildcard-imported)
            vap::ve_t       sC   enum_var   -> enum_typespec
            vap::vl_t       sD   logic_var  -> logic_typespec
            loc_t           sE   NOTHING    (module-local typedef)
            logic [3:0]     sF   logic_var  (the built-in arm, already right)
            vap::vq_t [1:0] sH   struct_var -> packed_array_typespec
        so the trigger is the WRITTEN QUALIFICATION, not the type's kind and
        not whether the name resolves for slang: a bare imported name and a
        module-local typedef both stay OUT of the def-view statement list
        (they still become struct_nets in every elaborated gen_scope).  The
        var class follows the PACKED-ARRAY ELEMENT kind — a packed array over
        a struct is a struct_var, not a packed_array_var — and row H also
        REPLACES what the older FuncAlias arm did for a qualified name (that
        arm's ref_var + UNSUPPORTED_TYPESPEC is right only for the BARE
        spelling, and is left in place for it).  Corpus: tlul_socket_m1.sv:90
        (tlul_socket_m1 + xbar_main).

  vc.sv  § hpSymbolicSelect + § hpSelParenStrip + § hpPartSelWsCompact
        (TypeEmit emitSyntaxExpr, the ScopedName hier_path arm).  THREE
        defects in one printer, found by following tlul_socket_m1 head by head
        as each one closed:
        (1) hpSymbolicSelect — the arm's literal cases key on ALL-DIGIT select
            text and its identifier case on a bare name, so `f[0+:A-B]`,
            `f[(B-B)+:C]`, `f[B-1:0]` and `g[B-1]` all fell to the final else,
            which names ONE ref_obj with the component's raw source text.
            This is the SAME BUG SHAPE pass 9 cut out of the sys-call argument
            loop and the gen-block port-actual dispatcher — a text-driven
            emitter's final else — at a third site.  Golden's shapes (element
            span always stops AT the closing bracket, as in the literal arms):
              [a+:w]/[a-:w]  indexed_part_select, VpiName = member,
                             ConstantSelect, IndexedPartSelectType 1/2,
                             Base_expr + Width_expr
              [l:r]          part_select, VpiName = member, ConstantSelect
              [x]            bit_select, VpiName = member, VpiIndex — and this
                             one spans the BRACKET CONTENTS (parens included),
                             not `<member>[…` the way the others do
            A DIRECT literal bound constant is UNPARENTED; one nested inside
            an operation keeps its operation parent.  Bound reads scope
            through the whole path plus the member
            (`work@m.blk.in_i[i].f[0+:A - B].f.A`) and a bound that IS one ref
            drops the member repetition — fullnames only, cmp does not read
            them, matched for byte-identity.
        (2) hpSelParenStrip — Surelog RE-LEXES the display name off its
            rebuilt tree, which has no ParenthesizedExpression node, so every
            parenthesis written inside a select DISAPPEARS from the name:
            `[0+:(A-B)]` -> `[0+:A - B]`, `[(B-B)+:C]` -> `[B - B+:C]`,
            `[(B-1):0]` -> `[B - 1:0]`, `g[(B-1)]` -> `g[B - 1]`.  Display
            only — `raw` keeps its offsets, which every element's location
            arithmetic reads.
        (3) hpPartSelWsCompact — the re-lex does not merely decline to ADD
            spaces around `+:`/`-:`, it DROPS whatever the source wrote:
            `a_source[IDW-1 -: STIDW]` reads `a_source[IDW - 1-:STIDW]`.  Same
            class as § basedLiteralWsCompact.
        vc.sv's DEF-view region is BYTE-IDENTICAL over all seven rows.
        Corpus: tlul_socket_m1.sv:97 and :105 (tlul_socket_m1 + xbar_main).

  vd.sv  § genCondQualPkgParamFold + § genCondBarePkgParamFold (TypeEmit, the
        ScopedName and IdentifierName arms).  The SIXTH position of the
        package-parameter fold family: a def-view GENERATE CONDITION naming a
        package parameter.  § genCondImportFold9 already folded the BARE
        materialized-import spelling but only through defModImportParam and
        only for an INTEGER value, so `if (tlul_pkg::ArbiterImpl == "PPC")`
        stayed a ref_obj.  The substituted object is the package parameter's
        OWN constant copied verbatim (crossPkgBoundFoldConst9), which is what
        carries a STRING across as ct 6 / size 24 / `"PPC"` and a based
        literal as `8'd9` / DEC:9 / ct 1.  Matrix (vd.sv):
            A  vdp::ArbiterImpl (untyped string)  -> constant, ts string_ts
            B  vdp::NW (int)                      -> constant
            C  vdp::BW (logic [7:0] = 8'd9)       -> constant `8'd9` ct 1
            D  ArbiterImpl (bare, wildcard)       -> constant, WHOLE-name span
            E  vdp::TypedImpl (string-typed)      -> constant size 24
            F  a module-local localparam          -> ref_obj (control)
        The QUALIFIED form anchors the constant at the SCOPE QUALIFIER
        (`pkg::`) exactly like the enum-member substitution beside it; the
        BARE form spans the whole identifier.  Corpus: tlul_socket_m1.sv:168
        (tlul_socket_m1 + xbar_main — after this the whole tlul chain has no
        head of its own left and advances into the shared PTRV_W class).
        The same round widened crossPkgBoundFoldConst9: a declared type with
        NO bit width (a `string` parameter) has nothing to re-stamp against,
        so the source constant's own size stands where the re-stamp wrote 0.

  ve.sv  § castSizeParamRefBindFinal (UhdmExporter, design-final).  THE PTRV_W
        CLASS, UNTOUCHED FOR SIX PASSES AND THE BIGGEST ONE LEFT — CLOSED, and
        it was ONE NULL POINTER.  r10earl10p prints a def listing's
        Parameters() and Param_assigns() vectors side by side with each
        parameter's typespec, its Cast_to_expr and each Rhs tree; over the two
        Earlgrey designs it says every one of prim_fifo_async's 6 parameters
        and 6 param_assigns is IDENTICAL except one field: PTRV_W's
        int_typespec carries a Cast_to_expr ref_obj whose Actual_group is
        BOUND to the parameter in golden and NULL in ours.  int_typespec::
        Compare chases Cast_to_expr and ref_obj::Compare chases Actual_group,
        which is why the head reported as `parameter 'PTRV_W' vs <null>` with
        the module_inst as parent and why five passes read it as a population
        difference.  § stampCastSizeParamTs binds `up` only on the call that
        first mints the ref, and for a module-BODY localparam that call runs
        before the listing's parameter object exists — the DISTINGUISHER is
        that the same cast on a PORT-LIST localparam (`localparam int unsigned
        DepthW = $clog2(Depth+1)` in the parameter port list) IS bound on both
        sides.  Surelog binds the LISTING'S OWN parameter of that name, so the
        repair is a design-final pass by name within each listing that only
        ever fills a null and never rewrites a binding.  ve.sv (30 lines) is
        cmp-EQUAL.  Corpus: prim_fifo_async PTRV_W (dmi_cdc, dmi_jtag,
        prim_fifo_async, tlul_fifo_async, + the two tlul entries that advanced
        into it) and prim_filter_ctr CTR_WIDTH.

