RESIDUES MEASURED THIS PASS AND NOT IMPLEMENTED (each with a witness):
  * kk.sv — a TYPE-CAST struct-pattern member value in a package parameter.
    Golden DEF `int'(1'b1)` -> UINT:1 SIZE 64 no decompile; golden TOP ->
    UINT:1 size 16 (the member width).  Ours takes the existing type-cast arm
    (ExprEmit, measured on FuncStructValSimple's `bit'(CVA6ConfigCExtEn)`) and
    writes BIN at the member width.  So `bit'` and `int'` do NOT fold alike —
    decode the distinguisher (target kind? 1-bit vs wider?) before widening
    that arm.  0 corpus tests at f5fbd25; the SIZE-cast sibling IS landed.
  * ll.sv (earlier revision) — a PORT RANGE BOUND that substitutes an imported
    package localparam keeps the referenced parameter's CONSTTYPE in golden
    (`input logic [DiffWidth-1:0]` -> ct 7 for a `-`-folded DiffWidth) where we
    re-render UINT.  Same § srlgArithFoldSigned matrix, different consumer.
  * mm.sv (earlier revision) — a struct-pattern CONT-ASSIGN member constant
    (`'{data: 32'h0, mask: 4'h1}`) is HEX 32'h0 in golden's ELAB view and UINT
    0 in ours; and a read of an unpacked-array package parameter
    (`mp::InitHash[0]`) folds its bit-select to a constant in golden where we
    keep the select.  Both were masking the mm law and are cut out of the
    witness on purpose.
  * jj.sv — golden's pattern-operation ref_typespec is PARENTLESS (no parent,
